@Montresor --- After working on this project for a year, you cannot make any assumptions.  I threw my cable modem out the window because of this project.  Latency matters.  Latency is caused by distance (and wireless and cable modems -- but I digress).  The speed of light is constant.

@EggsAnyStyle [G4G] [INTP-A] We thought about that, but it took too much supervision to make sure we were not forgetting about underserved areas.  I think we came to the assumption that there will some fluctuations and adjustments until we find what our normal download patterns will be.  We don't want to knee jerk into anything.  When the game releases, I think we will get a good look at the download sources.  I hope to spend some time anaylizing that data.

@KC what bugs are most important to you?

Yes, on that note, if you are in the western united states, your download time will be the shortest it has ever been.  Please download the game in the next two hours and report back.  I am seeing 16 pools in the US West region..

My conclusion at this point is that the US West region does not have enough coverage to warrent it's own region.  I will take down the LAX system pool in a couple of hours.

@ZEKE ⚡
